{
  "_provenance": "Captured from a real tenant on 2026-10-15 through pm-ai's own Graph client: the first page of GET /me/onlineMeetings/{id}/transcripts for a recurring Teams meeting the PM organises, the online meeting found by the join-link lookup the adapter makes. Redacted before it left the machine. Ids come from HMAC-SHA256 under a random 32-byte key that was never written down, so the mapping cannot be reproduced, or confirmed by hashing a guessed real value: GUIDs come out v4-shaped, Teams ids keep their shape (`19:...@thread.tacv2`, `19:meeting_...@thread.v2`, `..._...@unq.gbl.spaces`), and online-meeting and other opaque ids keep their length and alphabet. People are mapped per user id: one id is one 'Person N' across the channel and chat fixtures, and `mentionText` and the text inside `<at>` carry the same label. Free text: every word is replaced by lowercase letters of random length (2 to 9) in its own script, digits become 0, and punctuation, spacing and HTML entities are kept. Kept as recorded: keys, value types, timestamps (the real instants), Graph enumerations (keys ending in Type or Status, `@odata.type`, `contentType`, `messageType` and the like), the JSON keys inside card attachments, HTML tag names and structural attributes. `href` and `src` become https://example.invalid/<token>; URL fields become https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/redacted/<token>, keeping `?$skiptoken=` where the original had one. Kept whole: all 20 rows, which arrive newest first. The occurrence of 2026-10-15 holds two transcripts that do not overlap, 08:33:21-08:39:41 and 08:46:21-09:02:20 UTC: transcription was stopped and started again within one meeting. The calendar slot of the occurrences was not captured. transcript_recorded.vtt beside this file is a real transcript body as Graph returned it, captured separately and redacted the same way for its words; its voices are 'Speaker 1' to 'Speaker 4', unrelated to any 'Person N', and its cue timings are as recorded. Which transcript it is, is not recorded.",
